  "summary": "At a Marina Bay Neighborhood Council mayoral forum, Richmond's five candidates split over the city's Flock ALPR system, which Police Chief Tim Simmons turned off in December after learning data was externally accessible. Incumbent Mayor Martinez and challenger Jimenez opposed continuing with Flock, while Anderson, Johnson, and Wassberg supported reactivating the cameras. The council is set to decide the cameras' future at its next meeting.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "In December, Richmond police Chief Tim Simmons turned off the city's ALPR cameras after learning that some of the data was externally accessible through a back-door software feature.",
      "paragraph_idx": 20
    },
    {
      "quote": "I believe that police need tools. I don't agree with Flock as a company. What they did was to make us violate our own sanctuary policies.",
      "paragraph_idx": 23
    },
    {
      "quote": "There are companies, surveillance companies, who do the same work as Flock but do it here in California.",
      "paragraph_idx": 24
    }
  ],
